# Colmeia - Plataforma e Dependencias

## Escopo

Este arquivo registra o foco de plataforma e a selecao de pacotes do
repositorio.

## Foco de Plataforma

- Supported targets: Android, Windows desktop, and Web.
- Native iOS development and distribution are discontinued; do not recreate
  the iOS runner or release tooling.
- Web is a supported delivery target, not a preview-only platform.
- Keep native APIs behind platform guards or conditional imports, and validate
  browser behavior as well as Android and Windows behavior.
- Use responsive layouts and support touch, mouse, and keyboard interaction.
- A runtime `kIsWeb` check does not make an unsupported import portable.
  Use conditional imports for native IO and browser-only implementations.
- Browser storage is origin-scoped and may be cleared or denied. Do not treat
  Web token storage as equivalent to a native OS credential vault.

## PWA Delivery

- Use the custom `web/pwa-worker.js` for static assets and Push, with the
  versioned artifact list produced by `tool/package_pwa.py`. Follow
  `docs/install/web_guide.md` for build and hosting commands.
- Bundle renderer, fonts and required assets locally. Cache Storage contains
  only static files, never tokens, authenticated responses, API or Socket data.
- Navigation fallback applies only within the application scope; missing
  assets must remain errors. Validate both root and subdirectory hosting.
- Keep the previous version usable after failed downloads. Activate updates
  only through user action, respecting active synchronization/export work and
  other tabs before deleting old caches.
- Request Push permission only after explicit user action. Keep VAPID private
  keys on the server; authenticated subscriptions belong to the current user.
- Push clicks pass through existing authentication and authorization guards.
  Disable/logout unsubscribes locally and reconciles pending server cleanup.
- Keep Web capabilities behind interfaces with inactive native adapters.
- Client build configuration and bundled environment files are public assets;
  never place server secrets or private VAPID keys in them.

## Dependencias Preferenciais

- `dio` para HTTP e interceptors
- `get_it` para injecao de dependencia fora da apresentacao
- `go_router` para navegacao
- `provider` para estado de apresentacao
- `result_dart` para fluxos faliveis entre camadas
- `shared_preferences` para preferencias simples
- `flutter_secure_storage` para tokens e dados sensiveis
- `package_info_plus` para metadados da app
- `flutter_dotenv` para ambiente e configuracao de build
- `logger` para logging estruturado quando o projeto precisar de camada propria
- `hive_ce` for native key-value caching (Android and Windows)
- `idb_shim` for transactional IndexedDB access on Web, behind `AppCacheStore`
- `path` e `path_provider` para diretorios de dados no VM
- `uuid` para identificadores tecnicos
- `crypto` para hashing e operacoes criptograficas pontuais
- `google_fonts` para tipografia do design system quando fizer sentido
- `intl` para formatacao de moeda, data, hora e numeros
- `brasil_fields` para mascaras e formatacoes brasileiras comuns
- `flutter_form_builder` e `form_builder_validators` para formularios e filtros
  dinamicos
- `zard` para schemas pequenos de validacao e value objects
- `syncfusion_flutter_charts` para graficos interativos
- `syncfusion_flutter_datagrid` para grids de relatorio com sorting e filtros
- `flutter_local_notifications` apenas quando um fluxo concreto exigir
  notificacoes locais
- `sentry_flutter` para erros e performance, com DSN fornecido via
  `--dart-define=SENTRY_DSN=`
- `mocktail` como biblioteca padrao de mocks em testes
- `socket_io_client` para o canal Socket `/consumers` do `plug_server`;
  transport behavior belongs to `project_data_domain.mdc`

## Dependencias Fora de Escopo

- Add `tray_manager` only when a concrete Windows product flow requires it
- Nao mantenha `flutter_lints` junto com `very_good_analysis`
- Nao adicione `syncfusion_flutter_core` diretamente sem uso explicito de API
- Nao adicione `protoc_plugin` sem pipeline real de protobuf
- Evite `mailer` no app cliente; prefira envio de email no backend
- Pacotes como `jose` devem entrar apenas quando existir caso de uso concreto

